    {
      "id": "apparatus",
      "html": "<h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span><span>Text from autopsy</span></span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "translation",
      "html": "<h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag</a></p>  <p>The 'prostatai' of Demeter: Gaios Orkeios, son of Gaios; Gaios Solpikios, son of Gaios; Leukios Kaulios, son of Leukios; Chairetios son of Chairetios; Lykon son of Nymphon</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "commentary",
      "html": "<h2>commentary</h2>  <p>The statue is one of three found together close to the coast at Contrada Borgelusa di Avola, in the immediate vicinity of the site of a first-century BC Roman villa (which had an earlier Hellenistic building underneath). The other two statues are Kore and a youthful Herakles. Demeter holds a huge torch in her right hand and piglet in left. The inscription lists five prostatai (guardians of the shrine)of Damater (Demeter). The first three names are Latin / Roman: Gaius Orceius, Gaius Sulpicius, and Lucius Caulius. Gentili (1954) records the discovery; a Roman villa was subsequently excavated in the immediate vicinity. Manganaro (2009) is the most recent discussion, dating the statue to the second century BC.</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "bibliography",
      "html": "<h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Gentili 1954 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001958\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001958</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 1977 159 ph <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001440\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001440</a>  </li><li> 1984 34.0981 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796</a>  </li><li> Bacci 1984-1985 713 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002175\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002175</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 2001 86 no.V <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001806\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001806</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 2009 114 ph <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001796\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001796</a>  </li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  "
    },
